        "id": "development-b55e9da60c4698ee",
        "title": "Roald",
        "text": "Roald is a village in Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county , Norway .\nThe village is located on the northern part of the island Vigra .\nRoald is about north of the city centre of Ålesund , connected via two undersea tunnels which opened in 1987 ( and will be going through extensive upgrades starting in 2008 ) .\nÅlesund Airport , Vigra is south of the village of Roald .\nVigra Church is located a short distance south of Roald .\nThe village of Roald has a population ( 2013 ) of 808 , giving the village a population density of .\nThe village of Roald was the administrative centre of the old Roald Municipality that existed from 1890 until 1964 .\nThe former municipality was later renamed Vigra Municipality .\nSince 1964 , it has been a part of Giske Municipality ."
      }
    ]
